{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/259220-the-pacts-no-drawbacks-for-advantaging-the-human","id":259220,"title":"The pacts: no drawbacks for advantaging the human?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-17T14:17:51-07:00","id":259220,"title":"The pacts: no drawbacks for advantaging the human?","content":"I am at this moment planning a demon the descent chronicle and reading the system for pacts, I find it really amusing how easy, powerful and useful they can be. But, here's my problem: if the pact is unbalanced toward the demon, the willpower cost increases, but if it is unbalanced toward the human, nothing happens, as stated at page 191 of the core book: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the contract is signed, the demon must expend Willpower to finalize the deal. The amount she must spend varies depending on the terms of the deal. For a completely balanced pact, the cost is one point of Willpower, but pacts are rarely balanced. For each point by which the total aspects on the demon's side of the pact exceeds the human's total, the cost is an additional point of Willpower. This limits how far a demon can weigh the pact in her own favor. If the human's aspect points total more than those of the demon's side of the bargain there is no additional Willpower cost, but few demons give more than they take. </div> </div> </div> Not to mention that the boons that the demon offers are not even his, but are innerently created by its own primum, no matter what their size is. Thus, the demon can create a pact that offers virtually anything to the human and just ask for petty things in return...and there is no drawback whatsoever for the human or the demon. So, if the demon has nothing to lose he can pretty much obtain even the smallest and simplest things just by promising the world to their bargainers and everything would be fine, no compromise and no additional cost for anybody.<br /> <br /> Is there a part I've been missing? If you've also noticed the problem, what are your house rules to rectify this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3888-freddymontana","name":"Freddymontana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T14:45:29-07:00","id":259245,"title":"","content":"I've been wondering the same thing myself. My head canon is that the GM sometimes notices when someone gets a ton of good luck and therefore giving the human too much can compromise cover but I'm not sure if that really works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/92-ramza","name":"Ramza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar92_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T17:25:00-07:00","id":259388,"title":"","content":"Here is a thought. If one abuses this too much they will come across one the gm has a plan for eventually. Planned to die of illness to inspire their child to be a great man..... Suddenly recovering will draw gm attention as the established infrastructure fails. Not something to be done more than once but enough to potentially make your demons be more cautious and look into their marks a little more than such small rewards entail.<br /> <br /> also if they make a pact for tiny things they roll for compromise every time and it can catch up with them in that regard as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T19:27:19-07:00","id":259433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/259220-the-pacts-no-drawbacks-for-advantaging-the-human?p=259245#post259245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been wondering the same thing myself. My head canon is that the GM sometimes notices when someone gets a ton of good luck and therefore giving the human too much can compromise cover but I'm not sure if that really works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's the thing; pacts are the safest way to patch your cover since it uses subroutines similar to embeds (one can argue that simply buying stuff is safer since it's &quot;acting in-cover&quot; but that's for another discussion) so, unless the &quot;ton of good luck&quot; directly interferes with an infrastructure it won't be a problem. The demon just have to be a little clever in its investments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">also if they make a pact for tiny things they roll for compromise every time and it can catch up with them in that regard as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pacts doesn't cause any compromise rolls, that's the point. Unless I've missed something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3888-freddymontana","name":"Freddymontana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T19:42:25-07:00","id":259440,"title":"","content":"I believe unless i misread the page a pact costs one point of willpower and causes compromise.<br /> <br /> Now that i double checked they were mentioning pacts being destroyed being a compromise (in the line they had mentioned pact destruction causing no real harm to human but costing demon willpower point and compromise my brain miss filed that line) but none the less often actions required for a pact would most likely be acting grossly out of character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T20:40:08-07:00","id":259469,"title":"","content":"Why would you waste future leverage by giving away the store? Certainly other demons will take notice that you are making deals that are too generous and consequences ensue. Selfish, paranoid liars generally assume everyone else is the same way and they sure as shit will want to know why you are acting unselfishly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T21:47:24-07:00","id":259506,"title":"","content":"So the initial question I had to ask myself was &quot;Why would players do that?&quot; and the answer was obvious-&quot;because a front loaded cover/cultist deal like that is great, particularly if the benefits granted by the pact convert over with the identity&quot;.<br /> <br /> So the next question I asked myself was &quot;why don't do demons do that, within context?&quot;<br /> <br /> Answer: Because nothing is creation ex nihilo.<br /> <br /> The two immediate problems that emerge come out as this: 1)The God Machine would notice a major shift of metaphysical properties like that, which several people have noted, but on a more sinister note<br /> <br /> 2)Pacts take the route of...well, not least resistance, but with a certain great expediency. It takes what the pact offers and makes it well and truly yours, it makes a clear and significant part of your identity from then on, but it does so in the quickest possible variant of reality within a realm of acceptable loss. If grandma dying is the fastest way for you to get thsoe resources, and her doing so doesn't bloody your hands, then grandma's going to die.<br /> <br /> So a heavily front loaded list of benefits runs a high risk of completely destroying several aspects of the pactee's life, aspects that aren't easily repaired by a cancellation of the pact, or even that and judicious use of Exploits.<br /> <br /> That <i>might </i>not seem like a problem for the demon, but a demon who's out to benefit has to be wary about how this will screw over deals in future, not to mention the fragility of a cover or cultist after the fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T21:54:48-07:00","id":259512,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, one other in game thing.<br /> <br /> No one but a child believes in getting everything they ever so cheaply.<br /> <br /> Blood has got to spill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T22:26:56-07:00","id":259546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/259220-the-pacts-no-drawbacks-for-advantaging-the-human?p=259512#post259512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yeah, one other in game thing.<br /> <br /> No one but a child believes in getting everything they ever so cheaply.<br /> <br /> Blood has got to spill.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble with getting Something from Nothing is that Nothing gets all its stuff from Somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T22:48:28-07:00","id":259552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/259220-the-pacts-no-drawbacks-for-advantaging-the-human?p=259469#post259469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you waste future leverage by giving away the store? Certainly other demons will take notice that you are making deals that are too generous and consequences ensue. Selfish, paranoid liars generally assume everyone else is the same way and they sure as shit will want to know why you are acting unselfishly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I always thought demons were fairly rare (since it's not really precised anywhere in the book, that's what I assumed) so it would be hard for them to notice the consequences of such pacts. Again, pacts are subtle. That's the point. Even demons would hardly see the difference between them and a strike of luck.<br /> <br /> Selfish, paranoid liars? You assume a lot about demons. Paranoid? Sure, they have GOD on their trail. But there are no particular reason for them to be selfish or liers (I don't consider acting in-cover as lies since it's a necessary evil).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)The God Machine would notice a major shift of metaphysical properties like that, which several people have noted, but on a more sinister note</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. Again, pacts are made because they get you an identity fast, and subtly. No matter how big and radical the shift is, nobody notices, not even the GM or angels. They even precise in the book that people not concerned by the pact quickly dismisses it as something normal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one but a child believes in getting everything they ever so cheaply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and everyone knows that someone who won at lottery or the price is right acts like a perfectly grown up adult.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3888-freddymontana","name":"Freddymontana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T07:50:28-07:00","id":259754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freddymontana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/259220-the-pacts-no-drawbacks-for-advantaging-the-human?p=259552#post259552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)I don't think so. Again, pacts are made because they get you an identity fast, and subtly. No matter how big and radical the shift is, nobody notices, not even the GM or angels. They even precise in the book that people not concerned by the pact quickly dismisses it as something normal.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2)Yes, and everyone knows that someone who won at lottery or the price is right acts like a perfectly grown up adult.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>1)Normally that's because the pacts are balanced out <i>enough</i>. When a demon loads their side, they compensate with willpower, going in and voluntarily covering the added zeros to the transactions. When a human has the loaded side, nothing is covering it, but humanity has weird fluctuations all the time(particularly if, metaphysically, it's balanced out somewhat by the demon's side. The more you push it though, the more the calculations don't add up though. I think, operating on the principles the in game universe works on, a large enough windfall garners God-Machine* attention.<br /> <br /> 2)Yes, and everyone knows that one person who got looks, fame, money, and kung fu for a low cost.<br /> <br /> I'm not being facetious, entirely. Everyone does 'know' someone like that. But confront them with that in reality and it becomes really suspect. If you've got a cover that looks the part, maybe, but Demons don't always have a Hollywood Executive in their back pocket. When the average person is offered the world, the average person doubts the offer because the reality of that actually working is ludicrous.<br /> <br /> People like their fantasies at a distance, behind screens and paper pages. People get more uncomfortable when their fantasies are staring them in the face, because fantasies inherently don't belong within reality. I mean, yes, some people get really lucky, and you can always believe in that. But people get scammed by Nigerian princes too, and you can always believe that too.<br /> <br /> PS: If you think the only thing demons lie about is their cover, you aren't reading closely. Demons tell a lot more lies than that.<br /> <br /> *Kept trying to say Dog-Machine here. Maybe the G-M came from Pugmire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T09:33:20-07:00","id":259810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/259220-the-pacts-no-drawbacks-for-advantaging-the-human?p=259754#post259754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)Normally that's because the pacts are balanced out <i>enough</i>. When a demon loads their side, they compensate with willpower, going in and voluntarily covering the added zeros to the transactions. When a human has the loaded side, nothing is covering it, but humanity has weird fluctuations all the time(particularly if, metaphysically, it's balanced out somewhat by the demon's side. The more you push it though, the more the calculations don't add up though. I think, operating on the principles the in game universe works on, a large enough windfall garners God-Machine* attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. I think this is a good explanation and a legit reason for demons to be careful in this regard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/259220-the-pacts-no-drawbacks-for-advantaging-the-human?p=259754#post259754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2)Yes, and everyone knows that one person who got looks, fame, money, and kung fu for a low cost.<br /> <br /> I'm not being facetious, entirely. Everyone does 'know' someone like that. But confront them with that in reality and it becomes really suspect. If you've got a cover that looks the part, maybe, but Demons don't always have a Hollywood Executive in their back pocket. When the average person is offered the world, the average person doubts the offer because the reality of that actually working is ludicrous.<br /> <br /> People like their fantasies at a distance, behind screens and paper pages. People get more uncomfortable when their fantasies are staring them in the face, because fantasies inherently don't belong within reality. I mean, yes, some people get really lucky, and you can always believe in that. But people get scammed by Nigerian princes too, and you can always believe that too.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant is that sometimes &quot;too good to be true&quot; works. People want their wildest dreams coming true so bad that if someone were to offer them on a silver plate they would probably sign the damn paper. Sure, it's very suspect, and the person will read the whole thing if she's not stupid. But if everything written is okay, why wouldn't they sign? You have to look at it from the perspective of someone that hasn't red a lot of fictions about demons and the devil. Very few non-religious people do believe in faustian bargains, so they won't believe they're making a deal with a demon so all the demon has to do is find a good excuse and everything is okay for both of them.<br /> <br /> Again, it's a question of the demon being a little clever in its investments. When I say &quot;the demon can create a pact that offers virtually anything to the human and just ask for petty things in return&quot; I mean he does it WISELY and in the GOOD CONTEXT. If the demon is careful enough, he can abuse it without any consequences for him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/259220-the-pacts-no-drawbacks-for-advantaging-the-human?p=259754#post259754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS: If you think the only thing demons lie about is their cover, you aren't reading closely. Demons tell a lot more lies than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>About what? When they are in cover they must act like it or else they compromise. When they are in demonic form...well, they don't have much to hide, they're freakin' demon! It is part of the themes of demon that none of their identity is really theirs. Under their cover they are creatures that were once single-minded constructs and gained their true &quot;personnality&quot; when they fell. Why would you lie when you are virtually...nobody.<br /> <br /> Do you mean the subtle magic of embeds or the fact that they can use human ignorance to bluff? Well, that's what it is; bluff. The demons don't have to use it if they don't feel like it, it is not part of their inherent nature, so considering them liers for that is a gross generalisation.<br /> <br /> Do you mean the pacts? It ties back with the issue here, the demons don't have to lie if they don't feel like it. I was disappointed when I saw that the authors of the book didn't come with a clever way to explain why the devil would always try to double-cross all his bargainers. In the common folklore it's easy; &quot;He's the devil, he's evil&quot; but here we are dealing with ambiguous creatures.<br /> <br /> P.S. Don't think I'm being rude or anything, I just like to be the devil's advocate.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3888-freddymontana","user":"Freddymontana","date":". 09-18-2014, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3888-freddymontana","name":"Freddymontana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T12:58:21-07:00","id":259978,"title":"","content":"Given some more thought I found an idea I like even more. Demons can't overload the human side of the bargain. The way pacts work is that the demon pulls off small parts of a person. The universe abhors a vacuum though and so these missing parts are &quot;filled in&quot; sort of like when you cash a soul pact and take over the hole where the person used to be. The demon has the power to influence what exactly &quot;fills them in&quot; which is where the benefit comes from. Without a hole to fill though the demon can't give a benefit, therefore you can't give more than you take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/92-ramza","name":"Ramza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar92_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T13:13:39-07:00","id":260005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/259220-the-pacts-no-drawbacks-for-advantaging-the-human?p=259978#post259978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given some more thought I found an idea I like even more. Demons can't overload the human side of the bargain. The way pacts work is that the demon pulls off small parts of a person. The universe abhors a vacuum though and so these missing parts are &quot;filled in&quot; sort of like when you cash a soul pact and take over the hole where the person used to be. The demon has the power to influence what exactly &quot;fills them in&quot; which is where the benefit comes from. Without a hole to fill though the demon can't give a benefit, therefore you can't give more than you take.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I also thought of that. At first it seems like an easy way out, but so far it's my favorite solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3888-freddymontana","name":"Freddymontana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T18:51:05-07:00","id":260255,"title":"","content":"Selfish, paranoid liars is what the core book calls them. They operate like real life covert agents, not a group of people known for their forthrightness or honesty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T08:10:23-07:00","id":261272,"title":"","content":"A Demon has the perfect ability to lie. Even the noblest of creatures will one day be presented with a situation where they feel they must deceive someone. Noble creatures often fail this test or feel self-loathing for succeeding in it. Demons however have an inherent advantage over most in this regard: they only smile if they want to. They can also choose to smile the sweetest grin at you when, if they were human, their face would be red with rage. Humans connect emotions with outward tells unconsciously, demons however only show emotional tells or even pain responses if they consciously choose to show them. This, in a life where you have to lie about what you are simply to survive, creates a paradigm that often lying is simply easier than truth-telling and coupled with eidetic memory, a demon can never be caught out lying by its own mistake. When you are <i>nobody</i> how else can you be <i>somebody</i> if you don't lie?<br /> <br /> Put another way: Your demon's name is Truth. Truth has a cover, her name is Sally. Sally lives in a dorm room with a roommate, her name is Rochelle, and has a neighbor named Samantha. But Truth needs to pact, she needs to improve Sally because living with Rochelle is dangerous. Rochelle sees her more than almost anybody so it's very possible that Rochelle could see something about Sally that's suspicious and so unravel Truth's cover. So, Truth decides that to improve Sally, he will take Samantha's pet cat.<br /> <br /> He could tell Samantha that he is a demon named Truth and that he is offering her a faustian bargain. Or, as Sally, he could tell Samantha that her psychology classes demand a survey experiment and if she could just answer these few simple, purely hypothetical questions, and then sign on the dotted line. He might feel regret, after all, he chose the name Truth but Samantha would not see that unless Truth decided that Sally should look like she was lying. All Samantha would see, even if she hooked Sally up to a polygraph, would be Sally telling her the truth. This is so powerfully true that there are less than a handful of ways to undo this across all the splats. (But you don't have those, so in the Core there is absolutely <i>zero</i> way to counteract the perfect deceptive ability of a demon).<br /> <br /> When you are faced with this ability to lie flawlessly, how do you <i>not</i> use it on a regular basis?<br /> <br /> I would think that a demon could, certainly, be altruistic enough to do everything in their power to avoid lying unless absolutely necessary. But that sounds more like a character concept to me, than a general principle that demons work under.<br /> <br /> P.S: Demon population has to be at least substancial enough to be significant, considering the existence of Agencies. One is named in the Seattle chapter; along with the demon who is its defacto leader: Comrade West and the Demon's Republic of Seattle. Less specific, but still hinting at high-levels of demon-on-demon interaction, are also present in the Sample Agencies section that begins on page 59.<br /> <br /> P. P. S: As the storyteller, I can tell you, that the biggest deterrent for players giving humans far to much in the pact is that it is so, so, so easy for the storyteller to make a story out of it. Ultimately you, the storyteller, control that character; not the player. If someone gets to powerful, to rich, to famous, to fast this can upset the status quo and that's what the God-Machine protects. That human is toast. Even if that doesn't burn the demon in any way, the mortal is dead, and so serves no further bane to your chronicle. Colloquial karma is a nice counter-balance to cheating the system, I think? Even better when it's suggestive of greater, cosmic consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T08:56:53-07:00","id":261279,"title":"","content":"I personally have a house rule.<br /> <br /> The Demon is off the GM's radar, so to speak, but the human party is not. If a human gains something, and loses something else, but both are of equal metaphysical value (pact cost) then the human's net fortune is the same. It's a minor shift in where their fortunes lie, but it slips under the radar. However, if a human gives up one thing and gains something much greater in return, then suddenly, from nowhere, this human's fortunes have improved, and that's suspicious. If you work a minimum wage job, and suddenly one day $100,000 is deposited in you bank account, the IRS goes &quot;Wait wait wait, someone go check this out&quot;. Same deal.<br /> <br /> So, in a Pact Contract, if the Human's side of the deal is Better than the Demon's, then the Demon has to make a compromise check with a penalty equal to the difference. I.E. The Demon takes the mortal's Cherished Pet (a papered show dog) (Cover, Medial, +2) Permanantly (+3). In return he gives the mortal Riches (Asset Greater +3), Bruce Lee quality Martial Arts skills (Asset Greater +3), and Improved combat reflexes (Brawl skill bonus +3). So, the Demon's side is +5, and the Mortal's side is +9. This is a heavy swing in the mortal's favor. So the Demon would have to check for Compromise (attracting the GM's attention) with a penalty equal to the difference, in this case making a Compromise check at -4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T23:28:34-08:00","id":301858,"title":"","content":"I can think of several reasons why demons don't just casually give away large amounts of boons for nothing:<br /> <br /> \u2022They're selfish, manipulative and paranoid. The idea of giving tremendous gifts away in exchange for very little would probably make most laugh their Covers off. The rest would only do so because they had an angle.<br /> \u2022It's easy to start drawing attention when you start drastically altering the lives of many people without the subtle machinations that usually accompany clever Pact-work.<br /> \u2022Another demon can steal or destroy those contracts and then you've given away a ton of stuff for very little compensation. True, that means the thief won't get a ton of compensation, but then they might also go and &quot;renegotiate&quot; the contract. You've just made it easier for a rival to gain some serious advantages.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, yes a demon can use pacts to give away fantastic wealth (of whatever form) and ask for little in return. This can, at best, backfire as everyone tries to take advantage of her or leverage that uncharacteristic generosity. When you start making people into champion mixed martial artists, millionaires and curing diseases, you might just attract attention. Every action has a ripple. Hunters might notice, other demons, or something even more dangerous.<br /> <br /> It's not impossible for a demon to be especially generous with pacts. It's unlikely that any demon will survive casual and careless use of such incredible powers, however. Where pacts are most powerful is in their planning, their ability to gain the demon much more than it costs her, and the ability to do so in a way that doesn't draw undue attention. If you make a pact to take an abusive marriage wherein the spouse has no family and few friends, you aren't likely to draw much scrutiny. The same pact to take ownership of a tycoon's spouse is much more noticeable. Even for beings as self-absorbed as demons, too much attention can be a very bad thing.<br /> <br /> Of course, then another demon might offer to take some of that attention off of you, for a price...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T13:57:05-08:00","id":303710,"title":"","content":"Every connection is a liability. Even humans know you don't get something for nothing, and if you teach them otherwise they'll want more for so little. Hope your willing to keep giving stuff out, because when you no longer do, well the God machine might. Especially if it means getting a lead on a demon. <br /> And then, why they hell should humanity get anything easily when demon's have to put themselves in danger just to continue having free will?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}